# The build context of .clusterfuzzlite/Dockerfile is the repository root (ClusterFuzzLite, and
# OSS-Fuzz's `helper.py build_image --external $PWD`, both build with it), and its
# `COPY . $SRC/linuxgsm-panel` takes everything in it, gitignored or not. Docker does not read
# .gitignore or .git/info/exclude, so without this file a local fuzz build copied the working
# tree's secrets into an image layer: data/ (secret_key, cred_key, panel.db), the .venv, .git and
# every worktree checkout under .claude/, each with its own data/.
#
# A pattern without `**/` matches only at the root of the context, so the key and database names
# are written with it: a nested worktree's data/cred_key is not caught by `/data`.
# The fuzz build needs only tracked files, and none of them matches a line below.
.git
.claude
/data
.venv
venv
env
node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/*.db
**/*.db-*
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.secret
**/secret_key
**/cred_key
**/panel.db
